{# ─── Intro ─── #}
<section style="background:#fff">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head split">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Roof painting in Cairns</span>
        <h2>Restore the sparkle to your home.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="right">
        <p class="lede">We understand the importance of using quality materials and will only use the quality products available to ensure your roof looks great and lasts for years to come.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p style="color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.6;max-width:78ch">A faded, cracked or mossy roof can impact both the curb appeal and the protection it gives to your home. Over time, weather can take a toll on your roof, with severe weather cracking or dislodging tiles, damp creating moss and lichen, and the sun dulling your original roof colour to something pale and bland.</p>
    <p style="color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.6;max-width:78ch;margin-top:14px">Quality roof restoration or roof repair is a cheaper and often better option than roof replacement, and MrPaint specialises in professional roof painting that will restore the sparkle to your home. Regardless of the type of roof — be it residential, commercial or industrial — MrPaint's roof painting company can guarantee quality work and satisfaction.</p>
  </div>
</section>

{# ─── Terracotta ─── #}
<section style="background:var(--bg-soft)">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="rooftype-grid">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Affordable roof painting Cairns</span>
        <h2 style="margin-top:14px">Terracotta Tiled Roofs</h2>
        <p style="color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.6;margin-top:22px">There are two main types of terracotta tiles used for roofs — unglazed and glazed. Unglazed tiles are the standard red you see across Cairns, but for a more modern and custom look, terracotta tiles can be glazed or painted any colour to suit your home.</p>
        <p style="color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.6;margin-top:14px">MrPaint are experts at terracotta roof tile painting, selecting the right colour and paint to create a flawless and cohesive new look for your home. Roof restoration will involve first inspecting and then repairing or replacing any loose or broken tiles.</p>
        <p style="color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.6;margin-top:14px">We then use high pressure hoses to clean any moss or dirt from your existing terracotta roof tiles, creating the perfect surface for your new paint to adhere to. Specialised equipment is then used to prime and paint the tiles for a smooth, clean finish that will last.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rooftype-img">
        <img src="/assets/images/work-window-trim-roofline.jpg" alt="MrPaint painter working on a tiled roofline in Cairns" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

