        <h2 style="margin-top:14px">Concrete Roof Tiles</h2>
        <p style="color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.6;margin-top:22px">Concrete is another popular material for roof tiles, which can suffer the same fate as terracotta. While very durable, dirt and moss can build up over time, while the effects of the sun can dull the original colour.</p>
        <p style="color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.6;margin-top:14px">MrPaint can repair or replace any broken tiles and then pressure clean them to remove any lichen or mould from the tiles. The final step is roof tile painting to refresh the old colour or to bring a new style to the house. The painting process is important to us and we will take the time to prep your roof before starting any work. This includes cleaning the surface and repairing any damage that may have occurred over time.</p>
        <p style="color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.6;margin-top:14px">We also specialise in slate roofing and have a team of experts who are experienced in working with this type of material. We will make sure your roof looks amazing and provides protection from the elements for years to come.</p>
