{# ─── Metal ─── #}
<section style="background:var(--bg-soft)">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="rooftype-grid">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Colorbond &amp; steel</span>
        <h2 style="margin-top:14px">Metal Roofing Service</h2>
        <p style="color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.6;margin-top:22px">Colorbond or steel roofing is growing in popularity across Cairns, as a durable and modern alternative to tiles. Whether you want to de-rust and refresh the original roof, or go in a new direction with a brand new shade, MrPaint can help.</p>
        <p style="color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.6;margin-top:14px">For metal or Colorbond roofs, it's important to fully clean the roof first, using an industrial pressure cleaner to break down any oxidation or rust and leave the roof with the best surface for the paint to adhere to.</p>
        <p style="color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.6;margin-top:14px">The roof must then be primed to give maximum bonding for the paint to stick to. A special spray paint gun is used to make sure the primer layer is as smooth and even as possible. Lastly, specialised roof paint designed for metal is carefully applied. There is an enormous range of shades that can be applied — from the classic red or greys, to more modern browns, greens and even very pale beige for the all-white Instagram look!</p>
        <p style="color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.6;margin-top:14px">We understand the importance of using top quality materials and will only use the best products available to ensure your roof looks great.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rooftype-img">
        <img src="/assets/images/work-eaves-high-access.jpg" alt="Painter working at roof height on ladder and plank access" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ─── Gutters & Downpipes ─── #}
<section style="background:#fff">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="rooftype-grid rev">
      <div class="rooftype-img">
        <img src="/assets/images/work-exterior-eaves-detail.jpg" alt="Painter detailing eaves and gutter line on a Cairns home" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Gutter cleaning</span>
        <h2 style="margin-top:14px">Gutters</h2>
        <p style="color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.6;margin-top:22px">One additional area that can be forgotten is the guttering system around your roof. Broken gutters that leak and gap away from the edge of the house roof need to be repaired, then can be painted a similar or complementary colour to the roof.</p>
        <p style="color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.6;margin-top:14px">MrPaint can work with you to get the roof look that you are after. All types of gutters — from box gutters or fascia gutters, from round or square — can be revitalised with the right paint job. MrPaint can paint all materials of gutters, from steel to aluminium to even vinyl. By ensuring that a good quality undercoat and primer are applied first, we ensure that the paint will last for years and not peel within 12 months.</p>
        <h2 style="margin-top:32px">Downpipes</h2>
        <p style="color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.6;margin-top:22px">Downpipes are an important part of the roof ecosystem of your house, and it is easy to underestimate how noticeable they can be and how they can affect the curb appeal of your home. Rusting or broken downpipes can cause your roof to lose its integrity and reduce its lifespan. They may even cause water to pool on the edges and surfaces of your roof. With damaged downpipes, water could leak into your roof cavity and cause further damage to your property.</p>
        <p style="color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.6;margin-top:14px">Replacing or repairing downpipes is a key aspect of roof restoration and once they have been properly repaired, they can be painted a range of matching, or complementary colours to your roof and gutter system.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ─── Choosing Colours ─── #}
<section style="background:var(--bg-soft)">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head split">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Affordable roof painting</span>
        <h2>Choosing Colours</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="right">
        <p class="lede">The roof is one of the largest visual elements of a home and when painting it, deciding what colour to go with can be a challenging process.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p style="color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.6;max-width:78ch">The style of the roof — from a substantial A-frame roof which dominates the house look and feel, to the more suburban-standard gable roof or even a modern flat roof — all contribute to the style of your home and play part in the colour decision.</p>
    <p style="color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.6;max-width:78ch;margin-top:14px">Where the roof is a large feature that dominates the style of the home, you might want to go with more muted or mid-tone colours in grey or brown. However, for a smaller roofline on a modern home you can go bold, with dark colours and strong lines — both popular roofing colours.</p>
    <p style="color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.6;max-width:78ch;margin-top:14px">The surrounds of your home should also be taken into account, with homes amongst trees or on rural properties suiting a gentler look that blends with the natural environment. Homes on the coastline can capture the feel of the sea with subdued blues and greens bringing out the tones of the ocean. More suburban homes should look to the general feel of the neighbourhood and decide if you want to blend in, or stand out.</p>
    <p style="color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.6;max-width:78ch;margin-top:14px">Once the roof colour has been chosen, make sure it is complemented with the guttering and downpipes that surround it. You can even call back the colour of the roof in simple ways across your property, with the colour reflected by the mailbox colour, or even the fence — for a cohesive, styled look that maximises curb appeal and increases the value of your property.</p>
  </div>
</section>

